Image Conversion Flow
Step 1: User picks image

User clicks "Pick Image" button or the ImageView
ActivityResultLauncher opens image picker with MIME type "image/*"
Step 2: File size validation

ImageConverterBase64.getFileSizeFromUri() checks file size
Rejects images larger than 2MB
Step 3: Get bitmap from URI

ImageConverterBase64.getBitmapFromUri() converts URI to Bitmap using MediaStore.Images.Media.getBitmap()
Step 4: Display image

Bitmap is set to ImageView
"Pick Image" button is hidden
Step 5: Convert to base64

ImageConverterBase64.convertUriToBase64() handles the conversion:
Gets bitmap from URI
Resizes bitmap to max 100px dimension
Compresses to JPEG at 60% quality
Encodes to base64 string with NO_WRAP flag
Base64 string is stored in vehicleTypeModel.imageBase64
Step 6: Display existing images

When loading existing data, ImageConverterBase64.base64ToBitmap() decodes base64 back to Bitmap
Resizes to 500px width for display